libhsakmt fmm.c, gfx803: restore the GPU mapping of an object that
va-reuse-defer.patch parks, so a late GPU access to the freed buffer hits
the parked pages instead of faulting on a reserved but unmapped VA.

WHY
---
KfdDriver::FreeMemory in the hsa-runtime calls hsaKmtUnmapMemoryToGPU before
hsaKmtFreeMemory. By the time a free reaches the park branch in
__fmm_release_locked(), the object's GPU page-table entries are gone
(mapping_count == 0). The park withholds the VA from the free-list, so the
VA is reserved and unmapped, and any GPU access to it faults with "Page not
present". Stock libhsakmt tolerates such a late access, because it recycles
the VA at once and the next owner maps it again before the next touch. The
park takes exactly that away.

A torch `x.double().cpu()` alloc/free churn loop shows it as a hard,
repeatable GPU page fault (write from TC, in free VA space just past the
most recently freed block) on ROCm 7.14 and 10.0, both with torch 2.13.
ROCm 6.4.4, which recycles VAs at once, does not fault and is data-correct.
A minimal HIP repro isolates it to the fmm: allocate and write a buffer,
hipFree it, then write it again from a kernel. With the parked VA unmapped
this faults; with the mapping restored the kernel writes the parked
object's still-resident pages.

WHAT
----
In the park branch of __fmm_release_locked(), when mapping_count == 0, call
_fmm_map_to_gpu(), the same path the allocator uses to create the mapping.
It issues MAP_MEMORY_TO_GPU for each handle again and sets mapping_count to
1, and the KFD driver flushes the GPU TLB on map. A second release of a
parked object is already a no-op through the `deferred` flag, and an object
that is still mapped needs nothing. A forward declaration of
_fmm_map_to_gpu() sits next to the one for fmm_defer_release(), because the
definition comes later in fmm.c.

va-reuse-defer-noremap.patch takes the _fmm_map_to_gpu() call out again: a
restored mapping that is still in place when the object ages out collides
with the next allocation the fmm places at that VA. The two stay separate
patches, so that each effect can be switched off on its own.

Applies to: rocm-systems release/therock-10.2, commit
43fa692e568e65a1fb84f2d1c74415b042839f10, after va-reuse-defer.patch.

VERIFIED ON REAL HARDWARE (gfx803 box, 2026-08-30) on ROCm 10.0, without
va-reuse-defer-noremap.patch: parktest (a kernel writes a freed, parked VA)
passes 2 of 2, against 2 of 2 faults with the parked VA unmapped. The
restored mapping and the object's content are intact.

NOT YET RE-VERIFIED ON REAL HARDWARE on ROCm 10.2. The build applies
va-reuse-defer-noremap.patch after this patch, so parktest does not apply to
the shipped chain. The D2H churn and vLLM checks in that patch's header
cover fmm.c as it ships.

diff --git a/projects/rocr-runtime/libhsakmt/src/fmm.c b/projects/rocr-runtime/libhsakmt/src/fmm.c
index 642580b58a..a9a9e95992 100644
--- a/projects/rocr-runtime/libhsakmt/src/fmm.c
+++ b/projects/rocr-runtime/libhsakmt/src/fmm.c
@@ -207,6 +207,10 @@ static const manageable_aperture_ops_t mmap_aperture_ops = {
 };
 
 static void fmm_defer_release(HsaKFDContext *ctx, manageable_aperture_t *aperture, vm_object_t *object);
+static HSAKMT_STATUS _fmm_map_to_gpu(HsaKFDContext *ctx,
+			manageable_aperture_t *aperture,
+			void *address, uint64_t size, vm_object_t *obj,
+			uint32_t *nodes_to_map, uint32_t nodes_array_size);
 
 /* A freed allocation whose VA is being withheld from reuse for a short while.
  * The KV object is kept in the aperture tree (so the area stays reserved and
@@ -3317,6 +3321,18 @@ static int __fmm_release_locked(HsaKFDContext *ctx,
 	    !object->is_svm_paged &&
 	    aperture->ops != &mmap_aperture_ops) {
 		object->deferred = true;
+		/* KfdDriver::FreeMemory (the hsa-runtime) calls
+		 * hsaKmtUnmapMemoryToGPU before it calls hsaKmtFreeMemory, so
+		 * by the time a free reaches the defer here its GPU mapping is
+		 * already gone (mapping_count == 0, PTEs removed). Re-establish
+		 * it, so that a lagging GPU access to the freed buffer hits the
+		 * parked pages instead of faulting on a reserved but unmapped VA
+		 * (stock tolerates such an access through near-instant VA+phys
+		 * reuse).
+		 */
+		if (object->mapping_count == 0)
+			_fmm_map_to_gpu(ctx, aperture, object->start,
+					object->size, object, NULL, 0);
 		fmm_defer_release(ctx, aperture, object);
 		return 0;
 	}
